Round 15 (2026-02-27)

What landed
- File changed:
  - `clang/aot/emit.c`
- Added self-tail-call lowering in compiled head `REF`:
  - In head mode (`aot_emit_node`, `tag==REF`), when `term_ext(term) == current_def_id` and `STEPS_ITRS_LIM == 0`, emitter now outputs `continue;` instead of `return aot_call_ref(...)`.
  - Non-self `REF` behavior unchanged (`aot_call_ref`).
- Wrapped each emitted compiled function body in `for (;;) { ... }`:
  - `env_cells` / `env_locs` are reinitialized per loop iteration.
  - `continue` re-enters the same compiled function without C recursion, preserving stack/base calling convention.
- Added emitter state `AOT_EMIT_DEF_ID` so head REF lowering can identify self-calls.

Why
- `gab_deriv` still had hard deopts from `CALL_DEPTH_CAP=97` even after previous residual cleanup.
- Root cause: self-tail recursion still went through `aot_call_ref`, increasing `AOT_CALL_DEPTH` and eventually bailing out.
- Self-tail call is semantically a restart of the same compiled case-tree with same `(stack, s_pos, base)`, so loop continue is a safe lowering that avoids C stack/depth growth.

